      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened May 13 1871, officially naming the town Potomac, likely inspired by the Potomac River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potomac%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Havana, Rantoul & Eastern narrow‑gauge railroad arrived 1876, turning Potomac into a grain and livestock shipping hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
